# Active UI line (mandatory)

**Default:** Slint on `main`. There is no second UI track in this product tree.

| Branch | Role | Binary / run |
|--------|------|----------------|
| `main` | Active Slint UI | `bash scripts/run-slint.sh` → `noviewlog-slint` |

## Session start (before any edit or branch)

1. `git branch --show-current` and `git status -sb`
2. Auto-resync per `git-workflow.mdc`: if on `main` and behind, ff-pull; if on a merged PR branch, `git checkout -B main origin/main` and delete the feature branch. Do not wait to be asked.
3. Product UI work → stay on or use a feature branch off `main`
4. **Do not** create/switch branches unless the user asked or the task clearly requires it
5. Confirm which binary you will build before compiling (`noviewlog-slint`)

## Hard rules

- Feature branches → base off `main`
- Do **not** implement desktop chrome outside `crates/noviewlog-slint/`

## Slint paths

| Task | Location |
|------|----------|
| Slint UI | `crates/noviewlog-slint/` |
| Slint run helper | `scripts/run-slint.sh` |
| Shared engine | `crates/noviewlog-core/` |

After Slint/engine changes: build/run Slint (`run-slint.sh` or
`cargo build --release -p noviewlog-slint`). See `slint-release-build.mdc`.
